Z||000011||Jay||05-08-2001||07:07 PM||||It's a MOMO knob for a standard car.  I had someone make a mechanism so that you don't have to push the button down (like in a stock automatic shifter).  Instead the entire knob pushes down and allows you to shift gears.  It looks cleaner than an automatic knob.  Basically it has a sleave with slots in it.  When you push down the top of the shifter pushes the plastic rod down and allows you to shift, but with the look of a standard knob.<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
